      "role": "user",
      "content": "I'm reviewing our HACCP plan for a large catering contract. Can you give me the specific temperature and time requirements for cooling cooked poultry, specifically to avoid issues with Clostridium perfringens?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For cooling cooked poultry, you must adhere to strict temperature and time controls to prevent *Clostridium perfringens* from growing. The general guideline is to cool the poultry from 135°F (57°C) down to 70°F (21°C) within two hours. After that, it needs to continue cooling from 70°F (21°C) down to 41°F (5°C) within an additional four hours. This two-stage cooling process is critical for safety.",
